{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019uyW8Sq8W4pMK2X2fEJnrA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CLAUDE.md\n2\t\n3\t<!-- Claude Code expands these imports at launch, so every session (and every subagent that\n4\tdoesn't set omitClaudeMd) starts with them. Other agents read AGENTS.md, which names the other\n5\ttwo files. -->\n6\t@docs/DOCTRINE.md\n7\t@AGENTS.md\n8\t@docs/PROGRESS.md\n9\t\n10\t## Claude Code\n11\t- Subagents load this file and its imports. A subagent that must not see the repository's docs\n12\t  (a benchmark author or judge, a blind brief writer) sets `omitClaudeMd: true` in its\n13\t  `.claude/agents/` definition, as the two asset-bench agents do.\n14\t\n15\t## Builds for playing and testing (from 2026-11-02)\n16\tThere is no hosted site: Vercel is retired. The user plays and tests three builds, each one\n17\tfile made here and handed over (`SendUserFile`), never committed:\n18\t- Browser: `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file` -> `target/web/shardfall.html`, one ~10 MB page\n19\t  with the gzipped wasm inside; it runs from `file://` in Chrome or Edge.\n20\t- Windows: `scripts/build-windows.sh` -> `target/x86_64-pc-windows-gnu/dist/shardfall.exe`.\n21\t- Linux: `cargo build --profile dist -p pav_app` -> `target/dist/shardfall`.\n22\t\n23\tKeep them current: when a merged change can alter the game (anything beyond docs, notes, tests\n24\tand helper scripts), rebuild the HTML and send it, and the `.exe` or Linux binary when the user\n25\tplays that one or asks.\n26\t\n27\t`vercel.json` stays only as a guard: `\"git\": { \"deploymentEnabled\": false }` stops the Vercel\n28\tproject, if it is still connected, from building any push. Don't deploy to Vercel, re-enable\n29\tits builds or add a build config back unless the user asks.\n30\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b664ff9f-3df3-486c-8cc6-7a0b3ccfba7c","uuid":"743bc78a-a9ef-4f98-a257-3e551607424d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:15.820Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211926__x6e380e/work/.research/shardfall/repo/CLAUDE.md","content":"# CLAUDE.md\n\n<!-- Claude Code expands these imports at launch, so every session (and every subagent that\ndoesn't set omitClaudeMd) starts with them. Other agents read AGENTS.md, which names the other\ntwo files. -->\n@docs/DOCTRINE.md\n@AGENTS.md\n@docs/PROGRESS.md\n\n## Claude Code\n- Subagents load this file and its imports. A subagent that must not see the repository's docs\n  (a benchmark author or judge, a blind brief writer) sets `omitClaudeMd: true` in its\n  `.claude/agents/` definition, as the two asset-bench agents do.\n\n## Builds for playing and testing (from 2026-11-02)\nThere is no hosted site: Vercel is retired. The user plays and tests three builds, each one\nfile made here and handed over (`SendUserFile`), never committed:\n- Browser: `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file` -> `target/web/shardfall.html`, one ~10 MB page\n  with the gzipped wasm inside; it runs from `file://` in Chrome or Edge.\n- Windows: `scripts/build-windows.sh` -> `target/x86_64-pc-windows-gnu/dist/shardfall.exe`.\n- Linux: `cargo build --profile dist -p pav_app` -> `target/dist/shardfall`.\n\nKeep them current: when a merged change can alter the game (anything beyond docs, notes, tests\nand helper scripts), rebuild the HTML and send it, and the `.exe` or Linux binary when the user\nplays that one or asks.\n\n`vercel.json` stays only as a guard: `\"git\": { \"deploymentEnabled\": false }` stops the Vercel\nproject, if it is still connected, from building any push. Don't deploy to Vercel, re-enable\nits builds or add a build config back unless the user asks.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019uyW8Sq8W4pMK2X2fEJnrA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
