{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WEBkexrMSSDY7Evy51Juqa","type":"tool_result","content":"# Working in this repo\n\n## Finish every change on main\n\n- When a `/goal` is complete, or a prompt has changed the repo, commit and\n  push to `origin/main` right away.\n- Pushing does not deploy. Vercel usage costs too much to build every\n  change, so Git deploys are off (`\"git\": { \"deploymentEnabled\": false }`\n  in `vercel.json`) and the site runs locally: `pnpm dev`, then\n  http://127.0.0.1:7417. Deploy to Vercel only when Michael explicitly asks,\n  for a major update: push with `deploymentEnabled` set to `true` (that push\n  deploys; check it reaches READY), then set it back to `false` in the next\n  commit, which does not deploy.\n- Work on `main`. If a branch is ever needed, merge it into main and delete\n  it (locally and on GitHub) in the same session. Never leave a local\n  branch, an unpushed commit, a stash, or an open PR behind.\n- Before starting work, run `git fetch --prune` and look at\n  `gh pr list`. Anything open gets resolved first.\n\n## Pull requests from others\n\nDecide each one; do not let it sit. Accept it (merge to main, delete the\nbranch), reject it (close it with a one-line reason), or replace it (close\nit, and land a better version on main that says which PR it replaces).\n\n## Keep it simple and clean\n\n- No dependencies, no build step, no generated files committed\n  (`data/games.json` is gitignored and rebuilt by `scripts/scan.mjs`).\n- Run `pnpm test` (or `node --test \"scripts/**/*.test.mjs\"`) before\n  committing code.\n- Delete what is no longer used instead of leaving it around.\n\n## When something goes wrong\n\nRoll back rather than leave half-finished work. Revert the commit\n(`git revert`) or restore the last good state and push that, so main is\nalways a working wall. Say what was rolled back and why.\ndocs/curation-2026-09-24.md\ndocs/curation-2026-09-28-new-ai-stuff.md\ndocs/curation-2026-09-28.md\ndocs/curation-2026-10-28.md\ndocs/import-registry.md\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md\ndocs/session-hub.md\n\ndocs:\ncuration-2026-09-24.md\ncuration-2026-09-28-new-ai-stuff.md\ncuration-2026-09-28.md\ncuration-2026-10-28.md\nimport-registry.md\nimports\nmultiplayer-plan.md\nsession-hub.md\nsuperpowers\n\ndocs/imports:\n2026-10-13-baseline-tests.txt\n2026-10-13-browser-checks.json\n2026-10-13-cinder-choir-and-threads-sites.md\n2026-10-13-drive-games.json\n2026-10-13-drive-games.md\n2026-10-13-final-tests.txt\n2026-10-13-github-audit.json\n2026-10-13-github-browser-checks.json\n2026-10-13-github-build-fingerprints.json\n2026-10-13-github-builds.json\n2026-10-13-github-corrected-dry-run.json\n2026-10-13-github-five-audit.json\n2026-10-13-github-five-games.md\n2026-10-13-github-import.md\n2026-10-13-github-lineage.json\n2026-10-13-github-living-details-check.json\n2026-10-13-github-packaging.json\n2026-10-13-github-plan.json\n2026-10-13-github-provenance.json\n2026-10-13-github-remote-heads.json\naccount.test.mjs\natlas.test.mjs\naudio-inventory.test.mjs\naudio-review-browser.mjs\naudit3d.mjs\naudit3d.test.mjs\ncatalogue.test.mjs\ncheck-libraries.mjs\ncheck3d.py\ncouch.test.mjs\ndates.test.mjs\ndeck.test.mjs\ndesktop-import.test.mjs\ndev.mjs\nexplore-browser.mjs\nexplore.test.mjs\nfill.mjs\nfill.test.mjs\nfilter.test.mjs\nframes.test.mjs\nfriends.test.mjs\nhub-check.mjs\nhub-client.mjs\nhub-client.test.mjs\nhub-pages.test.mjs\nhub.test.mjs\nimport-catalogue.test.mjs\nimport-hub-pages.mjs\nimport-matrix-runs.mjs\nimport-registry.test.mjs\ningest.mjs\nintake.test.mjs\nkit.test.mjs\nlayout.test.mjs\nlib\nlibraries.test.mjs\nlibrary-browser.mjs\nmatrix-runs.test.mjs\nmatrix3d.py\nmesh.test.mjs\nmigrate-added-dates.mjs\nnames.test.mjs\nnet.test.mjs\nparse.test.mjs\nrelease.mjs\nrelease.test.mjs\nretrofit.mjs\nretrofit.test.mjs\nroundup-boot.test.mjs\nscan.mjs\nseed-import-registry.mjs\nsession-browser.mjs\nsession-library.test.mjs\nsession.test.mjs\nshots.mjs\nsimilar.test.mjs\nsweep3d.py\ntimeline.test.mjs\nvendor-libraries.mjs\nviews.test.mjs\n267:If a game misbehaves in a frame, *Open on its own page* in its Details drawer\n287:Players is *Single player* or *Multiplayer*, and Multiplayer opens head counts\n422:record, **F** favourites, **O** opens a game on its own page, **/** writes a\n489:In short: the `hub:session` metas in the head, the small `session.js` client\n495:why, is [`docs/multiplayer-plan.md`](docs/multiplayer-plan.md).\n500:not a multiplayer game on the wall: each player plays alone.\n518:each with a player leaving, then the game on its own. `--record` writes the\n564:  on its own compared with the original.\n592:After the picks, **Random Mode** deals. The hub deals every game that declares `hub:session` and\n624:- While no game in the library declares `hub:session`, the reference games\n750:| `players` | `1–2`, `1–4`… only when a game has co-op or versus | the Players rail: *Single player*, or *Multiplayer*, which drops a menu of head counts (*4 players* finds every game that seats four). A game with no `players` is single player |\n\n2197\nMorrowglass-Living-Places.html\noriginal-Little-Ritual-coffee-for-a-little-world-2026-10-03-model-unknown.html\nFinal-Fantasy-VI-First-Fantasy-6-The-Ember-Under-the-Ice-2026-09-07-model-unknown.html\nSmash-TV-Big-Money-Big-Prizes-TV-The-Broadcast-Circuit-2026-09-24-model-unknown.html\noriginal-The-Living-Codex-The-Silent-Bell-2026-08-12-model-unknown.html\nFair-Cry-Five-FarCry5-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261029-1402.html\nFar-Cryin-Out-Loud-FarCry5-gpt-6.1-terra-ultra-20261029-1101.html\nFar-Feral-Five-FarCry5-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261029-1452.html\nFar-Out-5-FarCry5-gpt-6.1-terra-high-20261029-1350.html\nFar-Wilder-FarCry5-gpt-6.1-sol-high-20261029-1530.html\nHigh-Cry-FarCry5-gpt-6-astra-high-20261029-1023.html\nRare-Cry-FarCry5-gpt-6-astra-ultra-20261029-0952.html\nRough-Cry-FarCry5-gpt-6-astra-max-20261029-0952.html","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b664ff9f-3df3-486c-8cc6-7a0b3ccfba7c","uuid":"6090b5c8-b04a-4ac5-bb10-69ea1421074b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:26:05.985Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Working in this repo\n\n## Finish every change on main\n\n- When a `/goal` is complete, or a prompt has changed the repo, commit and\n  push to `origin/main` right away.\n- Pushing does not deploy. Vercel usage costs too much to build every\n  change, so Git deploys are off (`\"git\": { \"deploymentEnabled\": false }`\n  in `vercel.json`) and the site runs locally: `pnpm dev`, then\n  http://127.0.0.1:7417. Deploy to Vercel only when Michael explicitly asks,\n  for a major update: push with `deploymentEnabled` set to `true` (that push\n  deploys; check it reaches READY), then set it back to `false` in the next\n  commit, which does not deploy.\n- Work on `main`. If a branch is ever needed, merge it into main and delete\n  it (locally and on GitHub) in the same session. Never leave a local\n  branch, an unpushed commit, a stash, or an open PR behind.\n- Before starting work, run `git fetch --prune` and look at\n  `gh pr list`. Anything open gets resolved first.\n\n## Pull requests from others\n\nDecide each one; do not let it sit. Accept it (merge to main, delete the\nbranch), reject it (close it with a one-line reason), or replace it (close\nit, and land a better version on main that says which PR it replaces).\n\n## Keep it simple and clean\n\n- No dependencies, no build step, no generated files committed\n  (`data/games.json` is gitignored and rebuilt by `scripts/scan.mjs`).\n- Run `pnpm test` (or `node --test \"scripts/**/*.test.mjs\"`) before\n  committing code.\n- Delete what is no longer used instead of leaving it around.\n\n## When something goes wrong\n\nRoll back rather than leave half-finished work. Revert the commit\n(`git revert`) or restore the last good state and push that, so main is\nalways a working wall. Say what was rolled back and why.\ndocs/curation-2026-09-24.md\ndocs/curation-2026-09-28-new