{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XwJMufJfykR6grDCAd7pdu","type":"tool_result","content":"sheet: poke, hidden, z_fight, mirror, tiny. size_band: an object of a known archetype (the last\nword of its name in store/size_bands.tsv, else its first tag: table, chair, barrel, sword …) far\noutside its real size, e.g. a 32 cm table; the line gives a scale op. socket_missing: a weapon\nneeds grip, a seat (chair, stool, bench, throne) sit. A hang socket hangs the object from it;\nwall_mount puts its back (z 0) on the wall. Sheets also take views=[front,top,30], elevation= and tile=.\n`asset_spawn action=add name=x pos=[x,y,z]` places a copy in the world. Saves go to\nassets/props/workshop/name.json; a metre template's copy is in metres: send\n{\"op\":\"unit\",\"to\":\"cm\"} before centimetres. `copy from=X` writes the fork's lineage:\n`\"lineage\":{\"method\":\"edited\",\"origin\":\"import\",\"parents\":[\"X@rev\"],\"license\":\"CC0-1.0\",\"credit\":\"…\"}`,\nwith X's origin (`import` for an import, `agent` for own work), licence and credit; edits and\npublish keep it, a patch cannot set it, and a copy of a format-1 template stays format 1 without one.\n\n## Names and tiers\n\nBUILTIN/name (templates) and LIB/core/name are embedded in every build, the browser's too. A\nshipped pack (`props::store::SHIPPED`, today `kaykit_adventurers`) has its files in every build as\nwell, while its rows keep their own tier: game data and rooms may name these and the embedded\nones. Other packs (assets/props/lib/pack/) load on first use in native builds; assets/props/local/ (packs, and WORKSHOP_LOCAL/name copies of their assets) is\ngit-ignored, for sources whose licences forbid sharing. Each pack folder has an index.tsv that\n`assets` reads; `assets reindex=pack` (or `=templates`) rewrites it, keeping its note column.\nA pack's PACK.json holds its licence (lib/ takes CC0 and CC-BY, lib/core CC0 only); reindexing a\npack rewrites assets/props/CREDITS.md.\n\n`asset_edit action=publish name=x if_revision=R review=\"ok: …\"` puts a workshop asset into LIB/core\nafter you look at its sheet (views=true elevation=game) at revision R. It needs no check findings, a description (≤ 120\nchars), a category, 2-6 tags, references to BUILTIN or LIB/core only, core or inline materials\n(not MAT/workshop/), and at most 400 tokens\n(food, tool, signage), 600 (container, lighting, rock, vegetation), 800 (most) or 2,000 (town,\ndungeon). It writes lib/core/x.json, its index row and a review.tsv line at this revision (an\nedited core asset needs a new review); rebuild to embed it.\n\n//! Where assets live (docs/ASSET_SYSTEM_PLAN.md §9.1).\n//!\n//! Names: `BUILTIN/<leaf>` (the templates), `WORKSHOP/<leaf>` and `WORKSHOP_LOCAL/<leaf>`\n//! (saved edits), `LIB/<pack>/<leaf>` (library packs: read-only, copy one to change it). A bare\n//! leaf is a workshop asset. Tiers: embedded in every build, the browser's included (the\n//! templates and `LIB/core`), disk (other packs under `lib/`: native builds read them on first\n//! use), local (`local/`, git-ignored: packs and workshop copies whose sources' licences forbid\n//! sharing them) and the workshop.\n\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n\ninclude!(concat!(env!(\"OUT_DIR\"), \"/asset_data.rs\"));\n\n/// The embedded library pack.\npub const CORE: &str = \"core\";\n\n/// Where an asset is kept, and so which builds have it.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord, Hash)]\npub enum Tier {\n    /// In every build, the browser's included: the templates and `LIB/core`.\n    Embedded,\n    /// Committed packs under `assets/props/lib/`, read on first use by native builds.\n    Disk,\n    /// On this machine only (git-ignored): packs under `assets/props/local/`, `WORKSHOP_LOCAL`.\n    Local,\n    /// Saved edits, `WORKSHOP/` (native).\n    Workshop,\n}\n\nimpl Tier {\n    pub const NAMES: &'static [&'static str] = &[\"embedded\", \"disk\", \"local\", \"workshop\"];\n    const ALL: [Tier; 4] = [Tier::Embedded, Tier::Disk, Tier::Local, Tier::Workshop];\n\n    pub fn name(self) -> &'static str {\n        Self::NAMES[self as usize]\n    }\n\n    pub fn parse(text: &str) -> Option<Self> {\n        Self::NAMES.iter().position(|name| *name == text).map(|index| Self::ALL[index])\n    }\n}\n\nconst NAMES: &str = \"asset names are BUILTIN/name, WORKSHOP/name, WORKSHOP_LOCAL/name or LIB/pack/name\";\n\n/// Normalize a name: a bare leaf is a workshop asset; set prefixes are read in any case; packs\n/// and leaves are lowercase.\npub fn canonical(name: &str) -> Result<String, String> {\n    let segments: Vec<&str> = name.split('/').collect();\n    let (set, leaf) = match segments.as_slice() {\n        [leaf] => (\"WORKSHOP\".to_owned(), *leaf),\n        [set, leaf] => match set.to_ascii_uppercase().as_str() {\n            set @ (\"BUILTIN\" | \"WORKSHOP\" | \"WORKSHOP_LOCAL\") => (set.to_owned(), *leaf),\n            \"LIB\" => return Err(format!(\"LIB names a pack too: LIB/pack/name, e.g. LIB/core/{}\", leaf.to_ascii_lowercase())),\n            _ => return Err(NAMES.into()),\n        },\n        [set, pack, leaf] if set.eq_ignore_ascii_case(\"LIB\") => {\n            let pack = pack.to_ascii_lowercase();\n            validate_pack(&pack)?;\n            (format!(\"LIB/{pack}\"), *leaf)\n        }\ntotal 2836\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:19 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:19 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 379859 Nov  4 21:19 style100_back.json\n24:\"fit\": {\"Aeroplane_Walk\": [10,55], \"Akimbo_Walk\": [16,88], \"Angry_Walk\": [10,105], \"ArmsAboveHead_Walk\": [7,81], \"ArmsBehindBack_Walk\": [10,57], \"ArmsBySide_Walk\": [8,70], \"ArmsFolded_Walk\": [10,66], \"Balance_Walk\": [7,43], \"BeatChest_Walk\": [13,79], \"BentForward_Walk\": [6,33], \"BentKnees_Walk\": [7,65], \"BigSteps_Walk\": [11,146], \"BouncyLeft_Walk\": [11,56], \"BouncyRight_Walk\": [9,73], \"Cat_Walk\": [13,101], \"Chicken_Walk\": [19,126], \"CrossOver_Walk\