{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EUtGdbfNqRbgSpJ8kgMZL4","type":"tool_result","content":"---\n30:TASK.md asks for an original game inspired by the source, and that is a hard line. Take the kinds of mechanics and th\n---\n905\n14192 PLAN.md\n13:## 1. The game\n15:### 1.1 Pitch\n18:### 1.2 Genre and perspective (DECIDED)\n23:### 1.3 Pillars: every feature serves one of these\n29:### 1.4 Keep what makes the source distinctive, and improve it. Do not copy i\n42:### 1.5 Scope (DECIDED)\n51:## 2. What I verified by building the engine here (2026-11-04)\n55:### 2.1 Builds\n62:### 2.2 Browser flags: TASK.md's list does not work for this engine\n71:### 2.3 Hub harness: confirmed passing on an engine page\n80:### 2.4 Input in headless Chromium\n97:### 2.5 What the engine does not give you (you build it)\n113:### 2.6 What is in the asset store\n124:## 3. World bible and writing\n126:### 3.1 Setting\n129:### 3.2 Cast\n153:### 3.3 Writing style (TASK.md: \"a writing style similar to the source's\")\n175:### 3.4 Story in one paragraph\n185:## 4. Controls (DECIDED)\n240:## 5. Systems\n244:### 5.1 Movement\n247:### 5.2 Shooting\n250:### 5.3 Weapons (DECIDED: three slots, plus throwables and machete)\n273:### 5.4 Condition and jams (pillar 3)\n285:### 5.5 Damage and treatment\n297:### 5.6 Fever (pillar 3)\n306:### 5.7 Fire (pillar 1: the feature people will remember)\n337:### 5.8 Wind and weather\n342:### 5.9 Time of day\n345:### 5.10 Stealth and detection\n350:### 5.11 Vehicles (engine changes required)\n369:### 5.12 Companions (pillar 3)\n377:### 5.13 Enemy AI\n387:### 5.14 Guard posts and territory\n390:### 5.15 Safe houses\n393:### 5.16 Economy\n401:### 5.17 Map, GPS, monocular (pillar 2)\n408:### 5.18 Tapes\n411:### 5.19 Reputation\n414:### 5.20 Wildlife and people\n418:### 5.21 Saves\n424:### 5.22 Difficulty\n429:## 6. The world\n431:### 6.1 Terrain and view distance\n445:### 6.2 Sky\n448:### 6.3 Places (positions are metres, x east, z